 ## [Unreleased]
+
+- **Refuse incomplete middleware class renames.** Class and namespace changes stop when a literal bootstrap middleware target would be left behind, including computed alias keys, literal spreads, nullable calls and uncertain receivers. Unresolved maps/targets refuse unverified edits; named `::class` targets remain renameable. Contributed by @thinkycz.
+
+- **Keep namespace declarations in namespace edits.** Inline, bracketed and multiline PHP namespace declarations now follow their imports and references, with comments preserved. Contributed by @thinkycz.
 
 - **Navigate application middleware aliases.** Go to Definition on route or typed controller middleware names opens static alias registrations in `bootstrap/app.php`. Hover shows declared targets; references and unsaved edits retain exact source ranges. Multiple registrations and unresolved targets remain explicit without running the application. Contributed by @thinkycz.
 
